||| Build-time `builtinExecutors` — the device-discovery candidate list for
||| the backends compiled into this `libidrisml` (the `BACKEND` list). The
||| header below is this `HwExecutors.idr.in` template; the `builtinExecutors`
||| definition underneath is appended per build by the Makefile's
||| HWDEVICES_IDR recipe.
|||
||| This is the value-level mirror of the generated `HwConfig` `Linked`
||| instances: one `someExecutor` candidate per admissible (device, dtype)
||| cell of each linked backend. `availableExecutors builtinExecutors` then
||| EAFP-probes them and keeps the ones backed by usable hardware on this
||| host (e.g. a torch build drops `TMps` on Linux, `TCuda 0` on macOS).
||| A tape-only build lists only `TapeExecutor` — spelling an mlx candidate here
||| wouldn't typecheck (no `Linked (MlxExecutor _)`), which is the compile-time
||| linkage gate doing its job. See
||| `docs/develop/device-availability-gating.md`.
|||
||| `builtinExecutors` can't live in `HwConfig` (the Executor barrel re-exports
||| `HwConfig`, so it sits upstream of `Tensor`, where `SomeExecutor` /
||| `someExecutor` are defined). Hence a second generated module, downstream
||| of `Tensor`, re-exported by the notebook prelude.
|||
||| Do not edit the generated `HwExecutors.idr` — it is regenerated on every
||| build and is git-ignored. Edit this `.in` file (the header) or the
||| Makefile HWDEVICES_IDR recipe (the `builtinExecutors` definition).
module HwExecutors

import public Executor
import public Tensor

